The energy-loss, fluctuation and material code re-implements published Geant4 11.3.2 models (G4MuBetheBlochModel,
G4UniversalFluctuation, G4UrbanFluctuation, G4EmSaturation, G4IonisParamMat, G4DensityEffectData) in Python; Geant4
is distributed under the Geant4 Software License. Code first written in mu2e-crv-fastsim (commit f451d7b).

mu2efastsim/ebrem.py re-implements G4SeltzerBergerModel and G4Generator2BS (Geant4 11.3.2); mu2efastsim/emsc.py uses the
screened-Rutherford cross section of G4WentzelOKandVIxSection and mu2efastsim/eannihil.py that of G4eeToTwoGammaModel.
mu2efastsim/data/mott_G4MottData_11.3.2.npz holds the electron Mott/Rutherford fit coefficients (fMottCoef) of Geant4
11.3.2 G4MottData.hh (Boschini et al., arXiv:1111.4042; Lijian et al., Radiat. Phys. Chem. 45 (1995) 235), values
unchanged, distributed under the Geant4 Software License.
mu2efastsim/data/brem_sb_G4EMLOW8.6.1.npz holds the Seltzer-Berger tables of G4EMLOW 8.6.1 (brem_SB/br<Z>) for the
elements of mu2efastsim/materials.py, converted without change of values (SHA-256 of each source file inside); the
G4EMLOW data are distributed by the Geant4 Collaboration under the Geant4 Software License (geant4.org/license).

Mu2e-internal inputs (conditions, calibration and lookup tables, detector data) and physics results are not part of
this repository and must not be added to it.

The optional cry_tables/cry_device modules re-implement the published CRY 1.7 model (LLNL UCRL-CODE-227323).
The retained CRY redistribution and additional DOE notices are in docs/third-party/cry.txt. CRY is not Apache-2.0;
the distribution tables are external hash-verified runtime inputs, not repository contents.
